--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. lunex_video (bundled binary)

   File: src/main/resources/assets/enderframelib/natives/lunex_video.dll
   A native video decoding library, shipped inside the mod jar and
   extracted at runtime by client/renderer/WebMediaManager.

   This is a prebuilt binary and is NOT covered by the LGPL-3.0 grant
   above. It is redistributed as a separate work; its own license terms
   apply to it. If you redistribute EnderFrameLib, carry this notice
   with it.

2. yt-dlp (downloaded on demand, not bundled)

   Project: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
   License: The Unlicense (public domain dedication)

   When external web media and the allowYtDlp setting are both enabled,
   EnderFrameLib downloads the official yt-dlp release binary for the
   current platform from GitHub, verifies its SHA-256 digest against the
   release's SHA2-256SUMS file, places it in <game directory>/enderframelib/,
   and runs it as an external process to resolve YouTube stream URLs. An
   existing binary placed there by the user is used as-is. yt-dlp is not
   distributed as part of this mod, and EnderFrameLib does not self-update
   it (-U is not used). The download happens only when both settings are
   enabled; the process starts only when a YouTube source is actually used.

   yt-dlp is released into the public domain under The Unlicense. See
   https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/blob/master/LICENSE for the text.

